Ejercicio 2: Complete the advert template
Aquí organizamos la información de los cuadros (a-h) en el formato:

Title: (d) 2002 Vespa PX 125 – only £2,000

General description: (f) Nearly new and hardly used Vespa, only 22,000 km.

Specification (size): (h) It is big enough for two people to ride.

Condition: (b) Only a few small stone chips. (c) Full 12 month MOT.

Accessories: (e) It is supplied with one helmet.

Action: more details: (a) Please contact me at vespa@hub.com for further information.

Delivery: (g) Pick up only. No deliveries.

Ejercicio 3: Impersonal style
Two noun phrases: "Full 12 month MOT", "small stone chips".

Two imperatives: "Please contact me", "Pick up only".

One passive structure: "It is supplied with..."

Two uses of "it": "It is big enough...", "It is supplied..."

Página 2: 7.3 Difficult customer
Ejercicio 1: Order the sentences
El orden lógico del diálogo es:

b (Assistant: What kind of thing are you looking for?)

d (Customer: I'm looking for a T-shirt.)

f (Assistant: T-shirts are over there.)

c (Customer: I'll take this one.)

a (Assistant: How would you like to pay?)

e (Customer: In cash, please.)

Ejercicio 2: Complete the conversation
(Palabras: bought, exchange, here, prefer, receipt, refund, sure, thanks, would, wrong)

Customer: Hello, I (1) bought this T-shirt yesterday but it's the (2) wrong size. It's a bit big. Assistant: (3) Would you like to (4) exchange it for a smaller one? Customer: Actually, I'd (5) prefer to have a (6) refund if that's OK. I'm not (7) sure I like it that much. Assistant: OK, I can do that if you've got the (8) receipt. Customer: Yes, (9) here it is. (10) Thanks ever so much for that.

Ejercicio 4: Match shopping phrases
It must (f) about it. (Ojo: suele ser "It must be...", pero aquí encaja con "f" si es "It must be about it") -> Corrección: 1-c (It must be on the label).

You're the shop manager, (a) right?

I have to be (d) quick.

The scarves are (b) over there.

Don't worry (f) about it.

It says 'hand wash only' (c) on the label.

